#=====================================================================
# test/diag/tdglog.ref
#
# Reference-value data for PROGRAM TDGLOG (test/diag/tdglog.f).
#
# Routine under test : modern/diag/diaglog.f
# Reference source   : bin/nastrn.f (LOUT=3); mis/mesage.f (NOUT)
#
# DELIVERABLE -- used in Solaris; not executed by Blitzy.
# This file is reference DATA only.  It is NOT a *.f source and is NOT
# matched by the bin/linknas "*.f" build glob, so it is never compiled
# or linked.  It is read/inspected by the unit driver and the test
# harness in the developer's Solaris environment (csh + Sun f77).
#
# Expected verdict   : PASS: TDGLOG
#=====================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
#   TDGLOG verifies that the modern diagnostic writer
#   modern/diag/diaglog.f emits its formatted record EXCLUSIVELY to
#   logical unit 3 (LOUT) when diagnostics are enabled.  The hard
#   constraint (AAP 0.7.2) is: all diagnostic output goes to logical
#   unit 3 (LOUT) only -- never stdout and never a new unit.  This
#   reference encodes the output unit, the minimum record count, the
#   representative in-band code the driver emits, and the source
#   evidence that justifies unit 3 being the diagnostic sink.
#
# RATIONALE (evidence from bin/nastrn.f and mis/mesage.f)
#   * bin/nastrn.f makes logical unit 3 the NASTRAN log: after the
#     bootstrap CALL DBMINT it sets LOUT = 3 and opens unit 3
#     (OPEN(3,FILE=DSNAMES(3),STATUS='UNKNOWN')).
#   * mis/mesage.f shows the LEGACY MESAGE writer targets NOUT
#     (COMMON /SYSTEM/ IBUF,NOUT,... ; WRITE(NOUT,...)), i.e. the
#     legacy print stream (~unit 6), NOT unit 3.
#   * The modern writer therefore deliberately uses unit 3 / LOUT,
#     keeping new diagnostics off the legacy NOUT stream and off
#     stdout.  This reference pins OUTPUT_UNIT 3 as the contract.
#
# BINDING EXPECTATION
#   With diagnostics ENABLED (IDIAG non-zero), CALL DIAGLOG(9001)
#   writes AT LEAST ONE record to logical unit 3 (LOUT), to no other
#   unit, and never to stdout.  The output unit is exactly 3.
#
# EXCLUSIVITY (by inspection of modern/diag/diaglog.f)
#   Exclusivity to unit 3 -- never stdout, never a new unit -- is
#   additionally guaranteed by inspection of modern/diag/diaglog.f:
#   it contains a single write target = unit 3 / LOUT.
#
# CONSISTENCY
#   OUTPUT_UNIT and SAMPLE_CODE below MUST match the constants
#   asserted in test/diag/tdglog.f and the single write target in
#   modern/diag/diaglog.f (enabled => >=1 record on unit 3).  The
#   sample code 9001 lies in the reserved 9001-9999 new-diagnostics
#   MESAGE band (AAP 0.7.2).
#
#---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-readable key/value lines (whitespace separated, one per
# line).  These are the values the driver and harness parse.
#---------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT_UNIT 3
EXPECT_MIN_UNIT3_RECORDS 1
SAMPLE_CODE 9001
EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TDGLOG
